Z||000000||Flash Box||05-18-2000||04:54 PM||||OK, I have been going over the Fiero I just got about a week ago and I deceide to take it for a short drive (No tags on it yet). The drive was fine until I went to slow down to pull into the driveway and the car shut off and wouldn't start it kept backfiring so I thought that maybe it had jumped time, but on closer inspection I noticed that my coil isn't mounted and it was just laying under the air cleaner (That is why I didn't notice it before) I just slide it back up under it and it started right back up so I at least got the car pulled the rest of the way into the driveway. Upon further inspection the wiring harness to the coil has been rigged. I hate it when people halfa$$ jobs. Now my question; where is the coil suppose to mount at? The coil looks similiar to the one that is on my Camaro so I have a general idea of what the bracket should look like also does anyone know where I can get the wiring harness for the coil? It is a 1984 SE with the 4 cylinder. If anyone can scan me a  picture of the location and what the bracket should look like and e-mail it to me I would appreciate it. Thanks in advance for any help. <p>[This message has been edited by Flash Box (edited 05-18-2000).]||||reg||9
